              "text": "### Primary Official Sources\n\n* **Official 30th Anniversary Portal / M6a Product Page:**  \n  `https://www.30th.pokemon-card.com/product/m6a/`  \n  *(Also accessible via the root 30th portal: `https://www.30th.pokemon-card.com/`)*\n* **Official Pokémon Card Japanese Trainers Website:**  \n  `https://www.pokemon-card.com/`  \n  *Set Announcement / Features:* `https://www.pokemon-card.com/` (under news coverage for MEGA 拡張パック「30th CELEBRATION」)\n\n---\n\n### Meaning of the Second Numbering Namespace (`01/30`)\n\nIn the Japanese expansion **MEGA 拡張パック「30th CELEBRATION」 (Set code: `M6a`)**, cards **017/103 through 046/103** comprise 30 consecutive Pikachu cards, each featuring distinct illustration artwork created by 30 different artists from throughout Pokémon TCG history.\n\n* **`017/103`:** The primary card collector number within the main 103-card expansion sequence.\n* **`01/30` (or `30th-01/30`):** The subset index denoting its exact position inside the dedicated **30-card Pikachu subset** (「個性的なピカチュウのキラカードが30種類！」). Card `017/103` (illustrated by Ken Sugimori) is card 01 of the 30 Pikachu cards.\n\n---\n\n### Status of Exact Official Images for M6a 104–121/103, 124/103, and Mew G/R\n\n* **Cards 104–121/103 (Art Rares / AR):**  \n  * 104: Alolan Exeggutor AR\n  * 105: Moltres AR\n  * 106: Lapras AR\n  * 107: Articuno AR\n  * 108: Zapdos AR\n  * 109: Toxtricity AR\n  * 110: Morpeko AR\n  * 111: Drifloon AR\n  * 112: Chandelure AR\n  * 113: Lycanroc AR\n  * 114: Nidorina AR\n  * 115: Alolan Meowth AR\n  * 116: Scraggy AR\n  * 117: Galarian Meowth AR\n  * 118: Gholdengo AR\n  * 119: Kommo-o AR\n  * 120: Meowth AR\n  * 121: Ditto AR\n* **Card 124/103 (Special Art Rare / SAR):** Fuecoco ex SAR (ホゲータex SAR; distinct from any MF 011/040 deck print).\n* **Mew G/RGB and Mew R/RGB:** Secret rare unnumbered prints designed by YOSHIROTTEN, carrying the special rarity codes `G/RGB` (Green) and `R/RGB` (Red).\n\n#### Unresolved Gaps & Official Site Limitations:\n1. **Absence from `pokemon-card.com` Public Database:** Secret Rares (cards numbered higher than 103/103, including AR 104–123, SAR 124–133, and the secret unnumbered `RGB` Mew variants) are omitted from the public card directory at `pokemon-card.com/card-search/`. The official card database only catalogs the regular 001–103 set, the Classic Collection reprints (136–165), and the basic energies.\n2. **Promotional Previews vs. Secret Cards:** The official product showcase page (`30th.pokemon-card.com/product/m6a/`) displays preview images of select cards (such as FUR Mew ex 135/103 and FUR Mewtwo ex 134/103), but does not host public standalone URLs or card viewer assets for AR 104–121, Fuecoco ex SAR 124, or the unannounced Mew G/RGB and R/RGB cards. High-resolution digital scans of these cards originated via *Pokémon TCG Live* client data and marketplace pack pulls rather than hosted image URLs on `pokemon-card.com`. Exact direct URLs from the primary domain cannot be provided as they are not published there.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
          ]
